      "snippet": "Signal >> Blog >> Signal is Serious About Protecting Your Privacy Get Signal Help Blog Developers Our Mission Give Now Signal is Serious About Protecting Your Privacy Meredith Whittaker on 20 Nov 2026 Privacy is our mission; it’s why we exist, and we do everything we can to protect it. This means that we are restricting the latest AI agents built into mobile operating systems from potentially capturing and storing your Signal data. We’ve already had to do this once with Windows. Last year, we used screenshot blocking to prevent Microsoft’s Recall AI from taking and storing screenshots of your Signal messages on Windows 11 operating systems by default. 1 We will now be taking similar measures to restrict agentic systems built into iOS 27 and on Android versions where we can detect an AI assistant attempting to read your Signal screen. 2 The problem is similar to Microsoft Recall on Windows: Google and Apple are integrating agentic capabilities like Gemini Intelligence with Google Gemini and Onscreen Awareness with Siri AI deep into their operating systems. This is a significant move. Google (Android), Apple (iOS/macOS), and Microsoft (Windows) produce the three major consumer operating systems (OS), which comprise the environment that third-party developers – like Signal – build their apps to function and operate within. To put it differently, these three operating systems are the oceans in which Signal, and other applications, must swim; they dictate the conditions of life for the application ecosystem. Right now, these agentic AI integrations are changing this environment in a way that’s making it increasingly hostile to privacy. This is an existential threat to Signal, and our ability to responsibly uphold our mission. In order to gain access to information about you, these OS AI agents “scan” the information that’s on your screen. In doing so, your Signal data is captured, then made available to these agentic systems in order to allow them to answer your questions and do your bidding. The net result is that these AI capabilities in the operating system are undermining Signal’s ability to independently guarantee privacy. For over a decade, this guarantee has been backed by our tried and trusted open source code base and our formally verified encryption protocol. These have been scrutinized by some of the best security experts and hackers across the world, and shown to be robust. Now, in service of AI agentic capabilities, your sensitive data is being captured, stored, and made accessible to whatever local database or remote server an OS-level AI agent is using at that moment. All of this is outside of Signal’s control once the data has been captured, and imperils the privacy of all the participants in a conversation. So, we are blocking such capture by preventing screenshots in the app on iOS 27 and when AI assistants attempt to capture screen data on Android. 2 People who want the ability to take screenshots can disable this protection within ",
      "oneLineKo": "Signal, OS 내장 AI 에이전트의 화면 데이터 수집 차단",
      "summaryKo": "Signal이 iOS와 Android에 내장된 AI 에이전트(Gemini, Siri AI 등)가 Signal 메시지 화면을 스캔해 데이터를 수집하는 것을 차단하기로 했다. 이미 Windows에서 Microsoft Recall의 스크린샷 캡처를 차단한 전례가 있으며, 이번엔 iOS 27과 Android에서 AI 어시스턴트의 화면 읽기 시도를 감지해 스크린샷을 막는다. Signal은 OS 제조사들의 에이전트형 AI 통합이 앱 생태계의 프라이버시를 근본적으로 위협한다고 경고하며, 이를 실존적 위협으로 규정했다. 사용자는 필요시 이 보호 기능을 수동으로 해제할 수 있다.",
