      "snippet": "Hurried Announcement: Alessandro Masullo GRH | Math 216: Foundations of Algebraic Geometry Home About AGITTOC 2020 2011-12 course 2014 course 2015-16 course 2017-18 course Math 216: Foundations of Algebraic Geometry November 20, 2026 Hurried Announcement: Alessandro Masullo GRH Posted by ravivakil under Uncategorized [2] Comments Hi everyone, I am at the American Mathematical Society Executive Committee and Board of Trustees meeting now, and about to chair an hours-long meeting, but this is urgent, so I will try to get this out quickly. Alessandro Masullo has a proposed proof of GRH, and Brian Conrad has been looking closely at it for months and gave extensive feedback which is being incorporated, and it is so far looking good. It is all human, with no AI. The hope was to bring Alessandro to Stanford for a year to polish the writing and then announce it after running it by enough people. Now it seems best to put out the current draft. I hope people quickly check it, formalize, fill any small gaps if they occur. I really hope it works. I have great faith in Brian’s judgement, and Brian has put a lot of thought into checking what Alessandro has done. There is a long story to tell, but right now I want to get the file out. Here it is. The Music Of The Primes Download Share this: Print (Opens in new window) Print Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window) Email Like Loading... Related 2 Responses to “Hurried Announcement: Alessandro Masullo GRH” Matt Says: November 20, 2026 at 11:11 am Great post! Thank you for advancing the state of the art in math. If you ever need website help or tech support, I’m your guy. You can have my direct number. P.S. “Great post, call me about your website” is exactly what Akismet was built to stop. If this lands in spam, I know a guy. 🙂 Reply AI claimed a solution to the 167-year-old Riemann hypothesis — and a human did, too - UK Daily: Tech, Science, Business & Lifestyle News Updates Says: November 20, 2026 at 4:12 pm