      "score": 356,
      "comments": 146,
      "snippet": "Unforced Euler singularity, unforced Navier-Stokes singularity, and the Generalized Riemann Hypothesis | What's new What's new Updates on my research and expository papers, discussion of open problems, and other maths-related topics. By Terence Tao Home About Career advice On writing Books Mastodon+ Applets Subscribe to feed Unforced Euler singularity, unforced Navier-Stokes singularity, and the Generalized Riemann Hypothesis 20 November, 2026 in math.AP , math.NT | Tags: AI , incompressible Euler equations , Levent Alpöge , Matei Coiculescu , Navier-Stokes equations , Riemann hypothesis , Tristan Buckmaster | by Terence Tao Obviously these results will be reported widely in other outlets, but I will note them here, in decreasing order of how “digested” the results currently are: Levent Alpöge, Tristan Buckmaster, and Matei Coiculescu, with heavy AI assistance, have written a human-readable proof of the finite time blowup for the unforced incompressible Euler equations in three dimensions , which is formalized in Lean here . Levent Alpöge and Tristan Buckmaster, again with heavy AI usage, have generated a proof of the finite time blowup for the unforced incompressible Navier Stokes equations in three dimensions, again with a Lean formalization . Here, the paper is technically human-readable and the general strategy of proof is broadly clear (following one of the expected paths to this result, namely to numerically build an approximate discretely self-similar solution and then use rigorous perturbation theory to convert this to an exact solution); but more work needs to be done to create a proper, professionally written proof. Levent Alpöge, using an internal AI model, has generated an (enormous) Lean-only proof of the Generalized Riemann Hypothesis. This Lean Zulip thread is probably the best place to follow the efforts to verify the proof and extract the strategy of proof (which, from very initial analysis, appears to use the full power of modern developments on the Langlands program and arithmetic geometry). (UPDATE: the moderators of the Lean thread are now focusing the discussion on the Lean-related aspects of the proof only.) I imagine the digestion process will take some time, though in this case at least we have a human author to communicate with to assist with this task. See also Buckmaster’s Mastodon post regarding the first two results. Share this: Print (Opens in new window) Print Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window) Email More Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window) WhatsApp Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window) Bluesky Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window) Nextdoor Share on Threads (Opens in new window) Threads Share on Tumblr (Opens in new window) Tumblr Share on Telegram (Opens in new window) Telegram Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window) LinkedIn Share on X (Opens in new window) X Share on Facebook (Opens in new window) Facebook Share on Reddit (Opens in new window) Reddit Share on Mastodon (Opens in new window) Mas",
      "oneLineKo": "AI 활용해 나비에-스토크스 특이점과 리만 가설 증명 발표",
      "summaryKo": "Levent Alpöge, Tristan Buckmaster, Matei Coiculescu 등이 AI의 도움을 받아 3차원 비강제 비압축성 오일러 방정식의 유한시간 blowup을 증명하고 Lean으로 형식화했다. 이어서 나비에-스토크스 방정식에 대해서도 유사한 blowup 증명을 Lean 형식화와 함께 제시했으나 아직 전문적인 서술이 더 필요하다. 또한 Alpöge는 내부 AI 모델을 이용해 일반화된 리만 가설(GRH)에 대한 방대한 Lean 전용 증명을 생성했으며, 이는 Langlands 프로그램과 산술기하학의 최신 성과를 활용한 것으로 보인다. Terence Tao는 이 결과들이 아직 충분히 검증·소화되지 않았으며 커뮤니티의 추가 검토가 필요하다고 언급했다.",
